# adjacency_attribsample

- Label: Attribute Sample with Adjacency
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/adjacency_attribsample.html
- Summary (EN): Converts a geometry attribute into a texture image packed into a UV atlas, so the attribute can be used as a map. It needs an adjacency cable and can sample a point attribute coming from another geometry.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme un attribut de géométrie en image de texture rangée dans l'atlas UV, à condition de brancher un câble d'adjacence.

- Inputs meaning: ["adjacency (required): adjacency cable from a Geometry to Adjacency COP", "attrib (optional): point attribute sampled from another geometry, for example from an Attribute Extract COP"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted and produced; 'Select Automatically' is recommended", "Attribute: geometry attribute name to sample (P gives a world-space position map)", "Class: Primitive, Point or Vertex"]

- Caveats: ["Requires an adjacency cable upstream from a Geometry to Adjacency COP", "Output type is determined automatically only when Signature is set to Select Automatically"]

